WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.863 --> 00:00:02.906
Line 3 runs in hall B.

2
00:00:03.574 --> 00:00:08.311
Now a new MES is coming, the system that runs the orders on the floor.

3
00:00:09.341 --> 00:00:11.802
You lead that IT project for the plant manager.

4
00:00:12.527 --> 00:00:15.093
The IT team builds the MES.

5
00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:19.583
We follow this one project through the four topics of the module.

6
00:00:20.273 --> 00:00:22.804
The details come later, in the lessons.

7
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.532
The first topic is the agile mindset.

8
00:00:27.313 --> 00:00:30.227
How do you build something the operators really use?

9
00:00:31.238 --> 00:00:36.079
In a waterfall approach the operators only see the MES at the end.

10
00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:39.793
Then it often turns out not to be what they need.

11
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.862
Agile works in short rounds, iterations.

12
00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:47.772
Each round delivers something small that really works.

13
00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:51.858
The operators try it out and the team adjusts.

14
00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:55.124
So you notice after weeks, not months.

15
00:00:56.112 --> 00:01:01.174
For the agile mindset we often use the Agile Manifesto and a hybrid approach.

16
00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:06.616
The second topic is Scrum, with roles, events and artefacts.

17
00:01:07.343 --> 00:01:09.340
How does the IT team work together?

18
00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:12.694
The team works in sprints of two weeks.

19
00:01:13.415 --> 00:01:17.780
Each sprint it finishes something usable, and then the next one starts.

20
00:01:18.768 --> 00:01:21.659
The Product Owner is the team lead of line 3.

21
00:01:22.342 --> 00:01:25.628
He decides what comes first, because he knows the floor.

22
00:01:26.638 --> 00:01:29.970
The Scrum Master helps the team and clears obstacles.

23
00:01:30.662 --> 00:01:33.077
The Developers build the MES.

24
00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:37.751
For Scrum we often use a Daily Scrum and a Sprint Review.

25
00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.619
The third topic is Backlog and estimating.

26
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.150
What do we build first, and how long will it take?

27
00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.165
The Product Owner puts all the work on one list.

28
00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:52.465
What delivers the most is often at the top.

29
00:01:53.516 --> 00:01:58.544
The team estimates the size relatively, by comparing with work it already knows.

30
00:01:59.557 --> 00:02:01.647
We are honest about the end date.

31
00:02:02.407 --> 00:02:05.368
We give a forecast with a probability and not a date,

32
00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.898
based on what the team really finishes.

33
00:02:08.916 --> 00:02:13.572
For Backlog and estimating we often use user stories and planning poker.

34
00:02:14.889 --> 00:02:16.990
The fourth topic is Kanban and flow.

35
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.695
How do you keep requests and faults from the floor moving?

36
00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:26.215
In Kanban every request or fault is a card that moves from left to right.

37
00:02:27.305 --> 00:02:29.534
A card that cannot move on is blocked.

38
00:02:30.279 --> 00:02:31.916
So you see where it stutters.

39
00:02:32.914 --> 00:02:35.898
The time from start to done is called cycle time.

40
00:02:36.562 --> 00:02:38.791
So you see how fast the work flows.

41
00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.699
For Kanban we often use a Kanban board and a WIP limit,

42
00:02:43.874 --> 00:02:46.254
a maximum of work in progress at once.

43
00:02:47.553 --> 00:02:48.714
It all connects.

44
00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:52.493
The agile mindset gives the reason, Scrum the rhythm,

45
00:02:52.633 --> 00:02:55.152
the list of work the order and Kanban the flow.

46
00:02:56.172 --> 00:02:57.948
Kanban starts where you are now.

47
00:02:58.661 --> 00:03:01.366
That is why it also fits alongside Scrum.

48
00:03:02.706 --> 00:03:04.413
This is the map of Projects.

49
00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:08.936
Agile and Scrum is the first station of IT and agile.

50
00:03:09.921 --> 00:03:13.508
Agile and Scrum has four topics, each with four levels.

51
00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:16.370
Start with the agile mindset.

52
00:03:17.158 --> 00:03:21.048
At Basics level it is about what agile is, the Scrum Team,

53
00:03:21.222 --> 00:03:23.382
user stories and the Kanban board.

54
00:03:24.418 --> 00:03:27.030
At Working knowledge you add the twelve principles,

55
00:03:27.216 --> 00:03:30.246
the events, refinement and WIP limits.

56
00:03:31.273 --> 00:03:36.544
At Advanced you add the roots of agile, the artefacts, velocity and measuring flow.

57
00:03:37.622 --> 00:03:40.954
At Expert you add the limits of agile, Scrum for real,

58
00:03:41.058 --> 00:03:43.891
forecasting from data and steering on flow.

59
00:03:44.897 --> 00:03:49.007
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
